<title>USA: U.S. wheat weekly export sales highlights -- USDA.</title>
<headline>U.S. wheat weekly export sales highlights -- USDA.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>USDA wheat export sales highlights in latest reporting week:</p>
<p>Net sales of 298,700 metric tons (MT) were off 27 percent from the previous week and one-quarter from the 4-week average.  The major buyers were the Philippines (127,100 MT), Taiwan (50,500 MT), Japan (34,300 MT), and South Korea (32,500 MT). Exports of 338,900 MT were 27 percent below the prior week and 5 percent less than the 4-week average.</p>
<p>The primary destinations were the Philippines (80,600 MT), Pakistan (67,900 MT), Mexico (37,400 MT), and Japan (34,400 MT).</p>
</text>
